From: Live ISO builder <live@localhost>
Subject: Fix a double free in get_fallback_session_name

ubuntu/prefer_ubuntu_session_fallback.patch frees "name" when the ubuntu
session is missing and then passes it to g_set_str(), which frees it again:
gdm aborts ("free(): double free detected") as soon as a user starts to log
in on a system that only has the vanilla GNOME session.
---
--- a/daemon/gdm-session.c
+++ b/daemon/gdm-session.c
@@ -639,7 +639,7 @@ get_fallback_session_name (GdmSession *self)
                 self->fallback_session_name = name;
                 goto out;
         }
-        g_free (name);
+        g_clear_pointer (&name, g_free);
 
         g_set_str (&name, "gnome");
         if (get_session_command_for_name (self, name, NULL, NULL)) {
